## A1·Synthesis — The Model AI Use-Case Intake Form (best-practice artifact)

Consolidating NIST MAP, ISO 42001 A.5, RAI Institute, Trustible, and published Microsoft/Google Cloud/AWS governance templates, a complete best-practice intake form contains the following fields. *For each: the field, why it is captured, and the decision it informs.*

**Section 1 — Use-Case Basics**
- **Title / one-line description** — indexing; portfolio view.
- **Proposer & department** — routing; ownership.
- **Tool/vendor proposed** (e.g., Claude Enterprise, Copilot) — security review path.
- **Problem statement (plain language)** — forces problem-before-solution; the reviewer's anchor.
- **Current process & quantified pain** (hours, error rate, complaint volume, cost) — baseline for later ROI; *do not skip — without it there is no denominator for value*.

**Section 2 — Proposed Solution & Scope**
- **Proposed AI capability / method** (drafting, summarizing, classification, retrieval, agentic multi-step) — maps to NIST Map 2.1; sets risk profile.
- **In-scope / out-of-scope** — prevents scope creep; clarifies the pilot boundary.
- **Integration & technical requirements** (connectors, data sources, systems touched) — security-review trigger.

**Section 3 — Data Needs & Sensitivity**
- **Data required** — feasibility input.
- **Data classification** (public / internal / confidential / restricted) — the single most important risk field; gates whether the use case is even permissible.
- **Data provenance/lineage** (NIST prompt) — IP and compliance.
- **Data availability & representativeness** (NIST Map 2.3) — data-readiness, the #1 scaling determinant.

**Section 4 — Value & Success Metrics**
- **Expected value** (hours saved, revenue/margin, error reduction) — prioritization input; maps to Map 1.4.
- **Success metrics / KPIs** — defines what "working" means; pre-commits the measurement.
- **Estimated investment / effort** — the denominator in RICE-style scoring.

**Section 5 — Risk & Compliance Flags**
- **Consequential decisions about individuals?** (hiring, lending, access, health) — escalates risk tier.
- **Customer-/member-facing?** — triggers transparency/disclosure obligations.
- **Regulatory tier** (EU AI Act-aligned: prohibited / high / limited / minimal) — legal path.
- **Personal/sensitive/regulated data?** — privacy review trigger.
- **GenAI-specific flags** — hallucination tolerance; autonomy/agentic scope; connector data-access breadth.

**Section 6 — Stakeholders & Oversight**
- **Business sponsor/owner** (single accountable) — decision rights.
- **Technical lead** — feasibility owner.
- **Legal / privacy / security contacts** — second-line reviewers.
- **Human-oversight model** (Map 2.2: where a human reviews/approves output) — the core appropriate-use control.

### A1·Process Mechanics (how the form behaves)
- **Conditional/branching logic** — low-risk requests (internal, no sensitive data, no decisions about people) answer a short path; high-risk requests unfold the full impact assessment. This resolves the rigor-vs-bureaucracy tension.
- **Triage SLAs** — acknowledge within ~2 business days; initial screen within ~5 business days; full evaluation within ~4 weeks. The published failure mode is "excessive bureaucracy" that drives shadow AI; speed is itself a control.
- **Routing & decision rights** — light-touch reviewer for low risk; full review board for high/novel risk (see A4).
- **Inter-rater reliability** — the Trustible/Leidos test: two reviewers, same submission, same decision. Achieved via defined rubrics for each scored field (see A2/A3).
- **Audit trail** — record which actions/criteria were applied and *why others were not*; NIST notes "the audit trail is itself a control."

| A1 framework | Origin | Core structure | Best for |
|---|---|---|---|
| NIST AI RMF MAP | NIST (2023) | 18 subcategories of context/risk | Defensible field completeness |
| ISO/IEC 42001 A.5 | ISO/IEC (2023) | Impact assessment + proportionate control | Certification / management system |
| RAI Institute Intake | RAI Institute | EU-AI-Act risk tiering + worksheet | Regulatory pre-classification |
| Trustible 4-category | Trustible | Basics / Risk / Value / Stakeholders | Usable form layout, triage speed |

